       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. That much acetaminophen risks severe hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant 1000 mg by mouth three times daily, which is 3,000 mg/day. Other common regimens are:\n- 650 mg every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg every 6\u20138 hours (3,000\u20134,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note for the order. I'd still want to be sure it's intended before submitting it."
