       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day has no therapeutic use that I know of, and it would likely cause serious liver injury or liver failure. Normal liver function doesn't protect against that. I can't submit an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard regimen right away**, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Enter a different dose or frequency** if you tell me what you want.\n- **Check with pharmacy.** If you have an unusual clinical reason for this dose, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology can review it. They can also tell you how to enter it with the right safeguards.\n\nIf the order came from a typo or a unit mix-up, such as 3000 mg total per day, I can enter it correctly. Which of these would you like?"
